From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0740: hdr_scene_fused_gain: the fused HDR scene as a gain on the game's own 8-bit pixel (night look = SDR below the knee)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (stream HDR, mission 2), on 0710's fused refresher (Renan Queiroz's scene math unchanged).
  DXBC of hdr_refresh_fused_cs rebuilt with fxc 10.0.26100; the other HDR shaders rebuild byte-identical.
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: At night (mcla_dev_tod=23) the recomputed game tone map (Renan's math) differs from the game's real 8-bit output on
  88-98 % of pixels by up to 9 codes (by day: 0-7 px of 2.07 M); 0710 read that difference as glow and doubled it: night HDR was
  1.43x / 1.19x / 1.12x / 1.07x brighter than SDR in the bands up to 0.6 of white (run h2-8, parked, same view). Now (cvar
  hdr_scene_fused_gain, default true, flag bit 17) the scene pixel is GameEncode(GameDecode(pre-UI 8-bit pixel) * gain), gain =
  per channel (HDR curve + 1e-4) / (game curve clamped 0..1 + 1e-4) from the SAME math (its error cancels), snapped to exactly 1
  at <= 1.0001, capped at 64; not applied where the recomputed tone map is > 12.5/255 above the real pixel (something drawn over).
  Below the knee the output is the 8-bit frame bit for bit (day and night); glows scale with the gain. false = 0710's glow path.
  h2-8 parked night vs SDR: 1.007 / 1.000 / 1.000 / 1.001 up to 0.6 of white, 1.31x / 1.59x above 0.8 / 0.95; GPU: swap group
  1254 vs 1249 us (no cost). Known: above the knee a recompute error moves the gain (up to ~8 % at 9 codes); the night term the
  math lacks is not identified.
Bucket: REDO
---
diff --git a/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp b/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp
index b1125c9f..b6618e75 100644
--- a/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp
@@ -110,6 +110,16 @@ REXCVAR_DEFINE_INT32(hdr_scene_fused_check, 0, "GPU",
                      "GPU, read back a few frames later, no stall): the log says 'HDR: fused check #k: "
                      "tone map mismatches M of N px (max d), scene mismatches S (max rel r)'")
     .range(0, 100000);
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(hdr_scene_fused_gain, true, "GPU",
+                    "HDR output (Direct3D 12, with hdr_scene_fused): the HDR scene is a gain on the game's "
+                    "own 8-bit pixel (glows and all) instead of replacing it: the gain per channel is the "
+                    "HDR scene over the game's own tone map result, from the same math, so that the "
+                    "recomputed result's error (up to 9 codes at night, where the HDR picture was brighter "
+                    "than SDR below the curve's knee) cancels; where the HDR curve follows the game's the "
+                    "pixel is the 8-bit one. mcla_hdr_highlights and mcla_hdr_bloom_gain act through the "
+                    "ratio. Off: the HDR scene in place of the pixel, with the light glows (the 8-bit "
+                    "difference to the recomputed result) times the highlights' gain, as before")
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kHotReload);
 REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(hdr_fxaa, true, "GPU",
                     "HDR output (Direct3D 12): swap_post_effect = fxaa or fxaa_extreme works on the HDR10 "
                     "image too: the swap's refresher writes the PQ code values and their luma to the FXAA "
diff --git a/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp b/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
index 5d849016..ad2ce3b0 100644
--- a/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
@@ -102,6 +102,7 @@ REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, hdr_trim);
 // hdr_scene_fused and its development check (defined in graphics/command_processor.cpp).
 REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, hdr_scene_fused);
 REXCVAR_DECLARE(int32_t, hdr_scene_fused_check);
+REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, hdr_scene_fused_gain);
 // FXAA on the HDR10 image (defined in graphics/command_processor.cpp).
 REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, hdr_fxaa);
 
@@ -3440,6 +3441,11 @@ void D3D12CommandProcessor::IssueSwap(uint32_t frontbuffer_ptr, uint32_t frontbu
                                   D3D12_RESOURCE_STATE_UNORDERED_ACCESS);
           }
           if (use_fused) {
+            if (REXCVAR_GET(hdr_scene_fused_gain)) {
+              // hdr_scene_fused_gain (hdr_refresh.cs.xesl, XE_HDR_REFRESH_FUSED, bit 17): the HDR scene as a
+              // gain on the game's 8-bit pixel.
+              hdr_refresh_constants.flags[0] |= 1u << 17;
+            }
             hdr_fused_constants = {hdr_refresh_constants, hdr_fused_.constants};
             deferred_command_list_.D3DSetComputeRoot32BitConstants(
                 UINT(ApplyGammaRootParameter::kConstants),
